.env
# Generated by test.py — build/score artifacts, same status as data/
test/

# Generated by calc.py — scored-submission artifacts, same status as data/
calc/

# Per-cell-type task fixtures pulled from /api/v3/tasks by search_hdr.py and the offline harnesses.
# Scratch inputs, not source: each is one round's contract + hbb_reference, refetched on demand.
# The hyphen matters — task.json is a tracked fixture and must stay so.
task-*.json

# CPU torch venv for seed_model/ (865 MB). Deliberately separate from .venv so the miner runtime
# never sees torch — see seed_model/README.md. The `.venv` rule above does not cover this name.
.venv-ml/

# seed_model checkpoints. Rewritten by every promoted refresh cycle, which round_plan.sh runs
# whenever a round stamps (~10/day), so tracking them means a ~6 MB binary diff per cycle for a
# file nothing reads back. seed_model/state.json is the durable record of the walk-forward score;
# a fresh clone regenerates the weights with `python -m seed_model.train --refresh` in ~65 s.
seed_model/**/*.pt

# Written by seed_watch.py — one JSON record per poll, appended forever while the watcher runs
# (30s x 3 tasks x 24h is ~2 MB/day, and it was already 1.1 MB when this rule was added). It is a
# measurement LOG, not an input: nothing reads it back, and what it establishes gets summarised into
# CLAUDE.md by hand. Tracking an append-only file means a whole new blob in every commit for content
# no clone needs. The script itself stays tracked — it is the reproducible part.
seed_watch.jsonl

# Research-harness output. The repo root is where ~40 offline harnesses drop their result JSON
# (`conj_*.json`, `win20_*.json`, `sd_sweep_*.json`, `validate_*.json`, ...) and 341 of them had
# accumulated as tracked files totalling 37 MB — `scores_fresh.json` alone is 30 MB. None is an
# input to anything: each is one run's numbers, and what those numbers ESTABLISH is written up in
# CLAUDE.md by hand, which is the durable record. Re-running the harness regenerates the file.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash so it covers ONLY the repo root: reports/, seed_model/, .claude/
# and niome_subnet/ keep their own JSON. Written as ignore-all-then-negate rather than 341 literal
# names so a NEW harness's output is ignored by default — being tracked by default is exactly how
# this pile built up. Add a `!` line for anything that is genuinely an input.
/*.json
# ...except these five, which are read AS INPUTS or are durable records, not outputs:
!/task.json             # a tracked fixture — see the `task-*.json` rule above, which spares it too
!/sd_task_listing.json  # /api/v3/tasks cache, read by ~25 harnesses via sd_task.fetch(cache=...)
!/sd_task_scores.json   # /api/v3/miners/scores cache, read by ~15 harnesses the same way
!/seed_window_log.json  # the accruing shadow log of window predictions, read by window_plan.py
!/hotkey_coldkey.json   # coldkey grouping, read as input by mingap.py / mingap_cells.py
